{
  "id": "geo-triangles",
  "chapterNumber": "3",
  "title": {
    "en": "Triangles &amp; Congruence",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The angles of every triangle sum to \\( 180^{\\circ} \\) — no matter its shape. Congruence criteria then let us prove two triangles identical from only three pieces of information.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Triangle facts",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Interior angles sum to \\( 180^{\\circ} \\). An <strong>exterior angle</strong> equals the sum of the two remote interior angles. Triangles are congruent by <strong>SSS, SAS, ASA, AAS</strong>, or <strong>HL</strong> (right triangles).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Drag the apex. The three interior angles change, yet their sum holds at exactly \\( 180^{\\circ} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "geoTriCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · The angle sum",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A triangle with a movable apex showing its three interior angles and their sum",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "geoTriDataBtn",
          "panelId": "geoTriDataPanel",
          "descId": "geoTriDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "geoTriDataRows",
